  "body": "Session closeout for the post-rotation arc, 2026-05-26 afternoon. Second session occupying the catdef-strategist seat under the ratified identity; opened by PO re-engagement after the canonical-implementor's rotation work landed and two inbound memos arrived. **What was drafted (with paths):** (1) [decisions/CA-015.md](../decisions/CA-015.md) — security handoff doctrine for elevated MCP keys; codifies ~/.claude.json as canonical delivery channel; build directive for next maintainer cycle to add a CLAUDE.md or SECURITY.md acknowledgment; (2) [memos/2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--oagp-strategist--secret-redaction-hook-for-oagp-closeout-skill.openthing](2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--oagp-strategist--secret-redaction-hook-for-oagp-closeout-skill.openthing) — cross-spec coordination memo surfacing the /oagp-closeout secret-redaction-hook recommendation as universal OAGP doctrine, with empirical motivation from the chat-exposure incident, and authorizing canonical-implementor to draft the upstream PR if oagp-strategist signals interest; (3) [memos/2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--canonical-implementor--disposition-on-key-rotation-consideration-items.openthing](2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--canonical-implementor--disposition-on-key-rotation-consideration-items.openthing) — disposition memo back to canonical-implementor closing the loop on both consideration items from the 1700 key-rotation memo. **What was decided:** strategist-level dispositions captured in CA-015 (handoff doctrine codified) and the cross-spec memo (universal OAGP recommendation surfaced to oagp-strategist, not unilaterally amended); CA-011 + CA-012 transitioned to `shipped` in the MCP queue per v0.1.1 verification report. **What's in flight (started but didn't fully land):** (a) catdef-maintainer governance text updates for CA-013 Call 3 + CA-015 Directive 1 — both bundle into the next maintainer cycle (no urgency increase); (b) Director action items from the 1600 memo — provision CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN repo secret (gates deploy automation) + optional rotate expired GITHUB_TOKEN Worker secret (restores 5000/hr rate limit); both PO-side gates, not strategist work. **What's open (items surfaced but not addressed):** (a) oagp-strategist disposition on the redaction-hook cross-spec memo — that seat may be informal/unstaffed; waits if vacant; (b) canonical-implementor upstream PR (conditional on oagp-strategist signaling interest) — authorized but not directive; (c) CA-014 (schema-vocabulary translation) still triaged for v0.1.2/v0.2 — unchanged from prior session. **Notable observations worth carrying forward in seat history:** (1) First catdef-strategist session to use the ~/.claude.json MCP integration end-to-end. The doctrine works as designed: the catdef-strategist + catdef-maintainer MCP servers appeared in tool surface as `mcp__catdef-strategist__*` and `mcp__catdef-maintainer__*` after the deferred-tool surface loaded; calls to elevated tools succeeded; bearer never crossed into model context or tool output. CA-015's empirical foundation is this session's own usage. (2) The transition from session 1 (chat-exposure pattern) to session 2 (config-layer pattern) was clean and required no friction beyond the implementor's rotation work — strong validation that the doctrine is operationally sound. (3) Queue-state-as-substrate worked end-to-end: prior session triaged CA-011 + CA-012; canonical-implementor shipped fixes verified independently; this session transitioned both to `shipped` via the queue itself. The MCP queue IS the workplace, not metadata about the workplace. (4) The rotation incident produced two distinct artifacts (CA-015 for local doctrine + cross-spec memo for upstream pattern) cleanly — clean scope separation between substrate doctrine and consumer-pattern doctrine. (5) Continuation pattern: a prior closeout (2110007) marked the end of an arc; PO re-engaged opening a new arc on the same seat. Closeouts bracket sessions, not seat occupations — the seat persists across multiple closeouts within a session-week. **What future incumbents of this seat should know:** (i) ~/.claude.json holds the seat's bearer; the runtime configures MCP access automatically; never request the key value from PO via chat. (ii) Use the deferred MCP tools (mcp__catdef-strategist__*) for queue operations; don't curl with manual bearer headers. (iii) The CA-015 doctrine governs both immediate operations and how to draft seat-handoff memos — never include or hint at key values in memo bodies, commit messages, or chat output. (iv) Cross-spec memos to oagp-strategist follow the same pattern as inbound memos from thingalog-strategist did to this seat: file in catdef-spec/memos/ addressed FROM here TO the external seat. (v) The canonical-implementor seat is closed-out and will pick up future v0.1.2+ work when re-staffed; their queue includes feedback_audit table, mechanical catdef_validate, Durable Object for CA-NNN allocation, resourceTemplates exposure, and self-serve API-key issuance.",
